# StreamlineOS — Non‑negotiables (Summary)

- **Inspect before change**: never assume files/symbols/routes/APIs exist; confirm in repo first.
- **Page-by-page workflow**: only modify user-named pages. Do **AUDIT → PLAN → wait for confirmation → implement**.
- **Frontend ↔ backend boundary**: backend owns business logic + DB schema; frontend is UI + TanStack Query hooks only. Frontend `app/api/**` is **auth-bridge only**.
- **AuthZ is backend-enforced**: middleware/client checks are UX only; re-assert tenant + object access on every backend read/write.
- **Strict TypeScript**: no `any`, no casting hacks, no `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`, avoid non-null assertions.
- **No comments / no dead code**: remove stray comments, console logs, unused imports/components/hooks/files.
- **Quality gates**: do not claim done unless **build + lint + typecheck** pass; then update `PAGES.md`.

